From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 20:28:16 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Eliminate hot-path boxing with fastutil primitive collections

Replace boxing java.util.HashMap keyed by Integer/Long on frequently
executed paths with fastutil primitive-keyed maps:

- EntityLiving.effects: Map<Integer,MobEffect> -> Int2ObjectOpenHashMap.
  Ticked every tick for every living entity (updatePotionEffects) plus
  per-tick hasEffect/getEffect checks. Key access now uses the primitive
  int API and the two hot iteration loops walk values() instead of
  boxing keySet entries.
- StructureGenerator.structureMap: Map<Long,StructureStart> ->
  Long2ObjectOpenHashMap. Long chunk-coord keys are outside the Long
  cache, so lookups previously allocated a boxed Long every time.

Adds the fastutil dependency. All touched lines marked // Athena.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

